{"item":{"candidateAnswer":"2019","evidence":"[D5:6 | 7:52 pm on 7 August, 2023] Sam: It looks like your kids are having a great time! And how long have you been prioritizing your health?\n[D5:7 | 7:52 pm on 7 August, 2023] Evan: Yes, they bring me such joy. My healthy road has been a long one. I've been working on it for two years now, so there have been ups and downs, but I'm doing my best.","itemId":"urn:uuid:1c53f79b-287a-5324-a949-112744b84891","provenance":{"sourceCommitment":"sha256:a644044079bc246357c97c066edfbe3f05446f629a7d38532ed909a01d15829b","timestamp":"2026-04-02T14:22:55Z"},"question":"Which year did Evan start taking care of his health seriously?","referenceAnswer":"2021","sources":[{"digest":{"sha256":"a644044079bc246357c97c066edfbe3f05446f629a7d38532ed909a01d15829b"}}]},"protocol":"https://spec.jinn.network/binary-judgment/item-bank-entry/v1"}
{"item":{"candidateAnswer":"build an indoor obstacle course for interactive play with his dog","evidence":"[D10:12 | 8:32 pm on 3 July, 2023] Andrew: Lately I've been finding new hobbies since I can't hike. I've been getting into cooking more and trying out new recipes - it's been enjoyable. Do you enjoy cooking? Any favorite recipes?\n[D12:1 | 10:05 am on 11 July, 2023] Andrew: Hey! So much has changed since last time we talked - meet Toby, my puppy. He's a bundle of joy and I couldn't resist taking him home, city living and all. How've you been?","itemId":"urn:uuid:1dd02e0c-7245-5f2e-846c-ef7d1a1ad80b","provenance":{"sourceCommitment":"sha256:d344620e2802fbae0735c6eba5e48447da69c6200dd95ec720e99d0dc188b692","timestamp":"2026-04-02T14:22:55Z"},"question":"What is an indoor activity that Andrew would enjoy doing while make his dog happy?","referenceAnswer":"cook dog treats","sources":[{"digest":{"sha256":"d344620e2802fbae0735c6eba5e48447da69c6200dd95ec720e99d0dc188b692"}}]},"protocol":"https://spec.jinn.network/binary-judgment/item-bank-entry/v1"}
{"item":{"candidateAnswer":"Various meaningful items from people she cares about","evidence":"[D2:7 | 9:49 am on 27 January, 2023] Deborah: It is love, and openness that have kept us close all these years. Being there for each other has made us both happy. Look what letter I received yesterday!\n[D2:9 | 9:49 am on 27 January, 2023] Deborah: The group members sent this to me! They thanked me for the positive influence I had on them. Those moments remind me why I'm so passionate about yoga.\n[D4:26 | 9:48 am on 4 February, 2023] Deborah: That's a really powerful message. It reminds me of someone special and their grace and strength when they faced hardships. Check out this creation!\n[D23:20 | 11:46 am on 30 August, 2023] Deborah: Exploring historical places and learning their stories is so fun. It was a great experience. I want to share this photo with you.\n[D23:22 | 11:46 am on 30 August, 2023] Deborah: This was written to me by a friend who, unfortunately, will never be able to support me. I miss him here. This quote says\"Let go of what no longer serves you.\"","itemId":"urn:uuid:1de8732c-a87c-5bad-8e36-362fc19d9e36","provenance":{"sourceCommitment":"sha256:b424143e1b4201522b36f827a0f7e649c59baa5abd3282abb8c6e90b0177619a","timestamp":"2026-04-02T14:22:55Z"},"question":"What gifts has Deborah received?","referenceAnswer":"an appreciate letter from her community, a flower bouqet from her friend, a motivational quote from a friend","sources":[{"digest":{"sha256":"b424143e1b4201522b36f827a0f7e649c59baa5abd3282abb8c6e90b0177619a"}}]},"protocol":"https://spec.jinn.network/binary-judgment/item-bank-entry/v1"}
{"item":{"candidateAnswer":"Unlikely, he seems very rooted in his community here","evidence":"[D24:3 | 3:34 pm on 17 July, 2023] John: I heard some cool stories from an elderly veteran named Samuel. It was inspiring and heartbreaking, but seeing their resilience really filled me with hope. It reminded me why I wanted to join the military.\n[D7:2 | 8:55 pm on 25 February, 2023] John: Hey Maria! Wanted to let you know that I'm running for office again. It's been a wild ride, but I'm more excited than ever! How have you been?","itemId":"urn:uuid:1ebefbe0-7f14-52d4-99aa-7fab86092156","provenance":{"sourceCommitment":"sha256:b35937df469c3b6f0e673df2e8be599b7b775d4564567914a397dbb31123151f","timestamp":"2026-04-02T14:22:55Z"},"question":"Would John be open to moving to another country?","referenceAnswer":"No, he has goals specifically in the U.S. like joining the military and running for office.","sources":[{"digest":{"sha256":"b35937df469c3b6f0e673df2e8be599b7b775d4564567914a397dbb31123151f"}}]},"protocol":"https://spec.jinn.network/binary-judgment/item-bank-entry/v1"}
{"item":{"candidateAnswer":"He speaks very highly of her and says she makes him feel energized and happy. He considers himself fortunate to have found her.","evidence":"[D5:1 | 7:52 pm on 7 August, 2023] Evan: Hey Sam, how's it going? Last week I went on a trip to Canada and something unreal happened - I met this awesome Canadian woman and it was like something out of a movie. She's incredible and being with her makes me feel alive.\n[D5:3 | 7:52 pm on 7 August, 2023] Evan: Woah. such a nice view! Thanks, Sam! She's definitely great. Every moment with her is really fun and energizing. It's a nice change, especially after dealing with health issues. But you never know what life's gonna throw at you. Btw look what life has thrown for me right now haha.\n[D23:3 | 1:32 pm on 6 January, 2024] Evan: Thanks, Sam! It was an awesome moment, and I feel really lucky to have found someone who gets me. Plus, our families are really happy for us - that's the best part!","itemId":"urn:uuid:1f9d15fd-fa2e-5c88-b3a6-95b60de0dd7d","provenance":{"sourceCommitment":"sha256:3636b2fc0e947a9571d4cbc0be65d240f8a5c2d93b006211d682469f52f10bf5","timestamp":"2026-04-02T14:22:55Z"},"question":"How does Evan describe the woman and his feelings for her that he met in Canada?","referenceAnswer":"He says she's cool, incredible, like something out of a movie, and that he feels alive around her. Every moment with her is fun and energetic, also Evan feels really lucky to have someone who gets him.","sources":[{"digest":{"sha256":"3636b2fc0e947a9571d4cbc0be65d240f8a5c2d93b006211d682469f52f10bf5"}}]},"protocol":"https://spec.jinn.network/binary-judgment/item-bank-entry/v1"}
{"item":{"candidateAnswer":"Mexico, Iceland","evidence":"[D16:9 | 5:13 pm on 9 July, 2022] James: I also love to read, especially while snuggled under the covers on a cold winter day. But now it’s summer and I want something more exciting! By the way, I bought air tickets to Toronto, and I’m leaving the day after tomorrow evening.\n[D17:22 | 9:49 am on 22 July, 2022] James: Everything went great! In addition, I even managed to get out to another country. The city of Nuuk, if you know. I stayed there quite a bit, but at least I had one more country to add to my bucket list!","itemId":"urn:uuid:20789e01-0866-5b06-9ede-7fdd9047c039","provenance":{"sourceCommitment":"sha256:d17316a7cb0f28d660f8427b36761e534412386c39834c6b2d35a76d0f2bdfb1","timestamp":"2026-04-02T14:22:55Z"},"question":"Which countries did James visit in July 2022?","referenceAnswer":"Canada, Greenland","sources":[{"digest":{"sha256":"d17316a7cb0f28d660f8427b36761e534412386c39834c6b2d35a76d0f2bdfb1"}}]},"protocol":"https://spec.jinn.network/binary-judgment/item-bank-entry/v1"}
{"item":{"candidateAnswer":"Early April 2022","evidence":"[D5:1 | 9:52 am on 12 April, 2022] James: Hey John! Long time no chat - I adopted a pup from a shelter in Stamford last week and my days have been so much happier with him in the fam. I named it Ned. Any progress on your gaming goals?","itemId":"urn:uuid:211ba5e0-ac8b-53f0-bd1e-283881926bba","provenance":{"sourceCommitment":"sha256:b63ce0b763d57067d6de5e79b265ca3c20ca94a052c41e82980b38ad7d05b7eb","timestamp":"2026-04-02T14:22:55Z"},"question":"When did James adopt Ned?","referenceAnswer":"first week of April 2022","sources":[{"digest":{"sha256":"b63ce0b763d57067d6de5e79b265ca3c20ca94a052c41e82980b38ad7d05b7eb"}}]},"protocol":"https://spec.jinn.network/binary-judgment/item-bank-entry/v1"}
